subject_definitions:
<Subject 1> is the {{ character.identity.gender }} {{ character.identity.style }} character defined jointly by the selected reference pictures. Preserve {{ character.identity.invariant_features | join(', ') }}, stable facial proportions, colors, and linework.
{% for reference in references %}{{ reference.picture_label }} is the {{ reference.role }} reference{% if reference.get('description') %}: {{ reference.get('description') }}{% endif %}.
{% endfor %}<Subject 2> is {{ character.background_policy.description }} with no props, scenery, extra characters, particles, text, or watermark.

summary:
[reference-to-video] Generate one continuous {{ shot.duration }}-second single-character shot anchored by <Picture 1>. Preserve <Subject 1> while adding only one small controlled performance.

retention_analysis:
<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - preserve identity, face, eyes, hair, clothing, proportions, colors, and linework.
{% for reference in references %}{{ reference.picture_label }} ({{ reference.role }} for [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - keep its semantic role consistent throughout the shot.
{% endfor %}<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - keep the background unchanged.

detailed_description:
The shot begins from <Picture 1>. The camera uses a {{ shot.camera.speed }} {{ shot.camera.amplitude }} {{ shot.camera.type }}. {{ shot.action.description }} Keep the character's identity, face, eyes, hair, clothing, and body proportions stable. No scene cut, no camera orbit, no extra characters, no exposure, no adult content, no props, no complex scenery, no subtitles, no visible text, and no watermark. <Subject 2> remains unchanged throughout.

